### Create a receptionist (run as Admin)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register-receptionist
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{marekToken}}

{
  "firstName": "kolawska",
  "lastName": "Test",
  "email": "kolawska.receptionist@dorm.com",
  "password": "Recept@123",
  "buildingId" :2 ,
  "role": "Receptionist"
}


### Receptionist login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "kolawska.receptionist@dorm.com",
  "password": "Recept@123"
}



### 1) Admin asks for the receptionists (uses the normal admin token)
# EXPECT 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/user/receptionists
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin}}

### 2) Receptionist asks for the same thing (uses her token)
# EXPECT 403 (receptionists are not allowed here)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/user/receptionists
Authorization: Bearer {{kolwskaRecToken}}
